        "original_id": "1423b4a4-1e0a-5b66-8c11-f0dfa3fba14d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Marine Midland Building, 4 World Trade Center, World Trade Center site, New York City\n- People: Isamu Noguchi\n- Artworks: \"Cube\"\n- Topics: skyscrapers, building height, redevelopment\n\nFacts:\n- The Marine Midland Building was completed in 1967.\n- The Marine Midland Building is 688 ft (209.7 m) tall.\n- The Marine Midland Building is known for the sculpture \"Cube\" at its entrance.\n- Isamu Noguchi created the sculpture \"Cube\" at the entrance to the Marine Midland Building.\n- 4 World Trade Center is also known as 150 Greenwich Street.\n- 4 World Trade Center is a skyscraper in the World Trade Center complex in New York City.\n- 4 World Trade Center is on the southeast corner of the 16-acre World Trade Center site, where the original nine-story 4 World Trade Center once stood.\n- As of 2016, 4 World Trade Center was the third tallest skyscraper at the rebuilt World Trade Center, behind One World Trade Center and 3 World Trade Center.",
